Local gfx906 signed-zero fix for Project Maya v1.1.41 (1710777).

Upstream already includes gfx906 registration, signed dot4 and transfer fixes.
Preserve Vega20's signed zero in INT8 latent-cache reads, retaining upstream's
gfx942/gfx950 exceptions. Both Vega20's F32 reference and FP16 product keep -0.

diff --git a/src/kernels/cuda/glm_lat8.cuh b/src/kernels/cuda/glm_lat8.cuh
--- a/src/kernels/cuda/glm_lat8.cuh
+++ b/src/kernels/cuda/glm_lat8.cuh
@@ -27,7 +27,8 @@ __device__ __forceinline__ uint2 lat8_q4(uint32_t w, __half2 d) {
     const __half2 bias = __halves2half2(__ushort_as_half(0x6480), __ushort_as_half(0x6480));   // 1152
     const __half2 a = __hmul2(__hsub2(*(const __half2*) &lo, bias), d);
     const __half2 b = __hmul2(__hsub2(*(const __half2*) &hi, bias), d);
-#if defined(STRATA_USE_HIP) && !defined(__gfx942__) && !defined(__gfx950__)
+    // Vega20's F32 reference preserves -0, as does its native FP16 product.
+#if defined(STRATA_USE_HIP) && !defined(__gfx906__) && !defined(__gfx942__) && !defined(__gfx950__)
     // a code 0 times a negative scale is -0 in FP16 and +0 through AMD's F32 product: a zero half loses its sign
     // (only a code 0 makes a zero here - a normal scale times any other code is a normal number).  CDNA3 and CDNA4 (gfx942, gfx950)
     // keeps the sign through the F32 product as NVIDIA does, so its FP16 product is already the same bits
